-- 008: RF (Руководитель филиала) daily-log task templates captured from the
-- real production screenshots supplied 2026-09-17 (Task 1, 3, 4, 5, 6 of the
-- РФ daily log). This is a pure data migration: no table shape changes.
--
-- Scope and honesty notes (do not remove):
--  * field_ownership_rules is set to "RF" for every field on all five
--    templates. That is directly evidenced for Task 1 (explicit "заполняет
--    РФ" badge). Tasks 3/4/5/6 did not show an explicit per-field ownership
--    badge in the captured screenshots; RF ownership is an assumption based
--    on these cards appearing on the РФ daily log, and must be corrected if
--    wrong.
--  * field_visibility_rules is left as '{}' (no extra readers) for every
--    field, including the "План на день" block on Task 1 that the screenshot
--    labels "видят РОП и РОО". field_visibility_rules is NOT YET READ by any
--    server code (grep-confirmed against src/domain/serialize.ts and
--    workItemService.ts as of this migration) -- storing a non-empty value
--    here would silently promise enforcement that does not exist. Extra-role
--    visibility for that block is therefore an open follow-up, not a
--    delivered feature.
--  * Several numeric fields shown in the screenshots as computed/greyed-out
--    (e.g. "Средняя стоимость ТС на складе", "Разница", RunRate on Task 6)
--    are modelled here as ordinary manually-entered number fields, because
--    the exact source formula was not fully visible/legible in the
--    screenshots. No calculation is implemented; a human must enter the
--    value. Flagged for correction once the real formula is confirmed.
--  * Task 2 (РФ) and the trailing fields of Task 6 (RunRate formula) were
--    illegible/cut off in the source screenshots and are intentionally NOT
--    included in this migration rather than guessed.
--  * ROP and ROO templates (from the "1-1"/"1-2"/"7,8,9" screenshot sets)
--    are NOT included here: role_permissions has no work-item grants for
--    ROP/ROO yet (only RF is seeded -- see migration 006), so creating
--    those templates now would let admins configure tasks nobody could ever
--    be assigned to own. That grant + the RF-only ownership-check
--    generalization in workItemService.ts is a separate, explicitly scoped
--    follow-up.
--
-- These templates are inert until an admin (or a follow-up migration)
-- actually creates work_items against them; inserting the template alone
-- does not create or assign any task, publish any KPI, or affect any
-- existing branch's history.

SET LOCAL search_path = pilot_r1, pg_catalog;

